MetaSplice Release 2.0 reproducibility package -- third-party content
======================================================================

MetaSplice's code, model, scores and derived tables are under the MetaSplice licence (LICENSE). The data tables also
carry values from the resources below, which keep their own terms. The wording of each licence and its source are
recorded in the MetaSplice repository (docs/FEATURE_LICENCES.md).

Variant sets
------------
ClinVar (NCBI): variants, classifications, review status and ClinVar identifiers, including the two release summaries
  in data/clinvar/. NCBI places no restrictions on the use or distribution of ClinVar data and asks that ClinVar be
  cited as the source. Landrum MJ, et al. Nucleic Acids Res. 2020;48:D835-44.
SpliceVarDB set (data/v2_variants_splicevardb.csv, data/v2_features_splicevardb.csv): variants and source studies,
  rebuilt for this study from SpliceVarDB's source studies with its published criteria (Sullivan PJ, et al. Am J Hum
  Genet. 2024;111:2164-75). The classifications are not included, except 14 extracted by hand from two studies
  (scripts/splicevardb/literature_classifications.csv); scripts/splicevardb/ restores the rest from the studies' files.
  Sources: Chong R, et al. Mol Cell. 2019;73:183-94 (MFASS); Shiraishi Y, et al. Genome Res. 2018;28:1111-25
  (SAVNet); Jayasinghe RG, et al. Cell Rep. 2018;23:270-81 (MiSplice); Casadei S, et al. Proc Natl Acad Sci USA.
  2019;116:26798-807; Fraile-Bethencourt E, et al. J Pathol. 2019;248:409-20.
  scripts/splicevardb/classify_all_datasets.py is the reconstruction's classifier, unchanged.
gnomAD v4.1 (the reference samples and the allele frequencies in the feature tables): CC0. Chen S, et al. Nature.
  2024;625:92-100.
Literature-confirmed splice-altering variants: gene and HGVS description of each variant, curated for this study from
  published reports.

Feature values in the tables
----------------------------
SpliceTransformer (Apache-2.0; You N, et al. Nat Commun. 2024;15:9129) and Pangolin (GPL-3.0; Zeng T, Li YI. Genome
  Biol. 2022;23:103) predictions, computed for this study.
DANN (MIT; Quang D, et al. Bioinformatics. 2015;31:761-3).
GPN-MSA (MIT; Benegas G, et al. Nat Biotechnol. 2025;43:1960-5).
phyloP and phastCons, 100-way and 470-way (UCSC Genome Browser; free for public and commercial use). Pollard KS, et al.
  Genome Res. 2010;20:110-21. Siepel A, et al. Genome Res. 2005;15:1034-50.
Gene level: gnomAD pLI and LOEUF (gnomAD; open data, with CC0 named for its primary data) and ClinGen
  haploinsufficiency scores (ClinGen; CC0), for HGNC's genes
  (HGNC; CC0), with the rules and values of the dbNSFP 5.4 gene file (Liu X, et al. Genome Med. 2020;12:103).
  scripts/build/gene_level/build_gene_level.py builds them from these sources.
Regions and exon context: GENCODE v50 MANE Select and MANE Plus Clinical (GENCODE/Ensembl; no restrictions). Harrow J,
  et al. Genome Res. 2012;22:1760-74. Morales J, et al. Nature. 2022;604:310-5.

Not included
------------
SpliceAI (Illumina; precomputed scores free for academic and not-for-profit use) and CADD v1.7 (free for
  non-commercial applications) scores. scripts/comparators/ rebuilds them from copies you obtain under their terms.
  Jaganathan K, et al. Cell. 2019;176:535-48. Schubach M, et al. Nucleic Acids Res. 2024;52:D1143-54.
